these grapes are ripe and  need to be picked but it's a risky  harvest this year  the situation in the north of the  israeli-occupied galan heights is tense  winemaker joao levy is worried about  more than his harvest  it's no longer safe here the fighting in  syria has reached us  rockets land here again and again  then everything is shut off but i do  trust our army to keep the situation  under control  of levi's vineyard is just a kilometer  from the syrian border  we hear repeated gunfire and see  exploded mortar shells  whether or not they were fired across  the border deliberately  the israeli army shoots back but  settlers like yo  of levi say this isn't enough  if we allow this to continue the  conflict will grow and get worse and  worse  the soldiers and extremists over there  should know that we will fight back  we have the ability we will  for israel the biggest problem at the  moment is not syria's assad regime  but the rise of islamist groups it's an  issue too for these israelis at kunitra  the only crossing between the  israeli-occupied golan heights and  syria they're debating whether it's  al-qaeda  is militants or the al-nusra front that  are on  israel's doorstep  it's all so close and really quite  frightening  you can almost see what's going on  without the need for binoculars  they're just walking around my gut  feeling is that things could explode at  any moment  it feels like the calm before the storm  there is growing concern that violence  could spill over from the civil war in  syria  especially after the attacks on the u.n  peacekeepers  right behind me in the buffer zone  between the occupied golan heights and  syria  not long ago fighters from the islamist  al-nusra front took control of the  syrian side of the kunitra crossing  and captured over 40 u.n peacekeepers  other units stationed there since the  mission began in 1974 fled to israel  the u.n has come under sharp criticism  because of this  this has been one of the quietest  borders of israel since  1974. the syrian side has fully  respected the ceasefire and so have we  and the peacekeeping forces actually did  not have much to do they were present  but they did not have much to do  now what can one infer from the fact  that those forces  fled uh once they started hearing  gunshots uh and actually we're not  fulfilling their mission  is those are complex lessons  people here say israel will need to  depend on itself for security  and keep a wary eye out for any  potential conflict  but observers say israel would not want  to see another front  open here in the north
 

